.TH tuarchitecture n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuarchitecture
.PP
Parses a Mermaid \fBarchitecture\-beta\fR block into a \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR model so an architecture diagram renders natively (SVG or PNG) through the pure\-Tcl engine everywhere \-\- no browser. Like \fBtuc4\fR, this is a \fBgraph parser\fR: it only builds a model; layout and rendering are done by \fBtudiagram\fR. Normally you call \fBtuflow::toSvg\fR / \fBtuflow::toPng\fR, which detect the \fBarchitecture\-beta\fR header, parse here, and lay the graph out.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tuarchitecture 0.1
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::tuarchitecture::parse text   ;# -> tudiagram model dict
.CE
.PP
Render the returned model with the tudiagram backends:
.CS
::tclutils::tudiagram::toSvg  model
::tclutils::tudiagram::toPng   model ?-scale n?
::tclutils::tudiagram::writeSvg model file
::tclutils::tudiagram::writePng model file
.CE
.SS "Supported syntax (Mermaid subset)"
.CS
architecture-beta
  group <id>(<icon>)[<Label>]            -> a group (flattened, see below)
  service <id>(<icon>)[<Label>] in <g>   -> a service node (`in <group>` optional)
  junction <id>                          -> a routing point (drawn as a dot)
  <id>:<S> -- <S>:<id>                    -> edge, no arrowhead
  <id>:<S> --> <S>:<id>                   -> edge, arrowhead at the target
.CE
.IP \(bu
The header is \fBarchitecture\-beta\fR (bare \fBarchitecture\fR is also accepted).
.IP \(bu
The display label is the \fB[Label]\fR, or the id if absent.
.IP \(bu
\fB<S>\fR is a side hint \fBL|R|T|B\fR; \fB\-\-\fR / \fB\-\->\fR / \fB<\-\-\fR / \fB<\-\->\fR choose the arrowheads (none / end / start / both).
.IP \(bu
Edge endpoints that were never declared are created as plain boxes, so an edge to an as\-yet\-undeclared id still renders.
.IP \(bu
Blank lines and \fB%%\fR comments are ignored.
.SS "Icons \-> shapes"
.PP
There is no external icon set; the \fB(icon)\fR maps to a tudiagram node shape so families stay readable:
.TS
l l.
icon	shape
\fBdatabase\fR, \fBdb\fR, \fBdisk\fR, \fBstorage\fR	cylinder
\fBcloud\fR, \fBinternet\fR	rounded
\fBserver\fR and anything else	box
.TE
.SS "v1 limitations (honest)"
.IP \(bu
\fBGroups are flattened.\fR A declared \fBgroup\fR is \fBnot\fR drawn as a container box, and \fBin <group>\fR is ignored for layout (tudiagram lays the graph out left\-to\-right). A group box is Phase 2. A group id that an edge references is drawn as a plain node.
.IP \(bu
\fBSide hints are not routed.\fR \fB:L :R :T :B\fR are parsed but do not steer the edge ports \-\- the engine decides port positions (the same limitation as \fBtuc4\fR's \fBRel_U/D/L/R\fR hints). The declared topology survives; the exact approach side may differ from Mermaid.
.IP \(bu
\fBIcons are shapes, not glyphs\fR (no Iconify dependency).
.SS Usage
.CS
package require tclutils::tuarchitecture
set src {architecture-beta
    group tier(cloud)[Application Tier]
    service web(server)[Web UI] in tier
    service api(server)[API] in tier
    service db(database)[Database] in tier
    web:R -- L:api
    api:B -- T:db}
::tclutils::tudiagram::writePng [::tclutils::tuarchitecture::parse $src] arch.png -scale 3
.CE
.PP
In Markdown, \fBarchitecture\-beta\fR rides on the \fB```mermaid\fR fence, so docir's raster sinks (pdf / odt / rendererTk) render it through \fBtuflow::toPng\fR; no docir change is needed.
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Companion: \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR (layout + render), \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR (dispatch). \fBtuflow::parse\fR delegates \fBarchitecture\-beta\fR here and returns the tudiagram model, exactly like \fBmindmap\fR / \fBC4*\fR / \fBgitGraph\fR.
.IP \(bu
Because it is a graph type, the same model also flows through every other tudiagram consumer unchanged.
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TCLUTILS TUARCHITECTURE <REASON>}\fR \-\- \fBEMPTY\fR (no services; a diagram consisting only of flattened groups also yields no nodes).
